# Pairs with RAllOrNothing, and shows that a receiver reader observing
# BETWEEN two prepare arrivals is in scope: RAllOrNothing is a state
# invariant, so it is checked in every state, including each one between two
# re-shipped prepares. The base exports a decision row for every saga the
# origin stores and its prepare seam settles a re-shipped pre-cut prepare
# against it (#4510), materialised on Committed and dropped on Aborted. The
# defect is in the export: a decided saga whose buckets have not drained yet
# is exported with its decision row but without committed rows for those
# buckets, so the receiver serves every key pre-saga under a committed
# decision. Each re-shipped prepare then settles its OWN key post-saga as a
# last-writer-wins write, and a reader between two arrivals sees one key
# post-saga and the other pre-saga. Exporting such a saga's resident buckets as
# committed rows (the base's ExportRow, #4510's export change) is what keeps
# the settle atomic. The omission is keyed to a saga NONE of whose buckets has
# drained, where every key is otherwise pre-saga, so the counterexample is the
# key-by-key window rather than a partial snapshot.
MODULE: RAllOrNothingSettleKeyByKey
TARGET: RAllOrNothing
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a decided saga's undrained buckets are exported without committed rows, so re-shipped prepares settle it one key at a time

--- FIND
    IF snap = "committed" THEN "post"
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: no committed rows for a decided saga none of whose buckets has drained.
    IF snap = "committed" THEN (IF \A j \in XKeys : pend[T][j] = "pending" THEN "pre" ELSE "post")
--- END
